      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This has been a pet peeve of mine for nearly a year now, and would be great to be able to address via the labs system. It's been a self reinforcing spiral, where one world author will have their own personal world volume set lower than usual, and tailor their world to their own settings rather than the default. Thus all visitors are forced to reduce their own, and are less likely to increase them again. They then make their own worlds tailored to those settings, and the problem gradually amplifies. \n\nWhen I first joined the game I kept my volume settings at the default 100% for months, but now I feel compelled to keep them around 40%. Which is frustrating because in any world where the author is being reasonable with volume, it throws off the balance of any more subtle audio design such as background ambience, which might be entirely missed at that volume.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5cfe98a7bff97a7f22183a8d",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5b0d59b48096a127bde0735b",
