      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5cfba5e04ee5ca62e21f9cf4",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What you miss here is how everyone has different type of audio devices and also different audio settings in windows which is always gonna lead to a different results in attempts to come up with settings for the volume in the worlds anyway\n\nHaving 100% \"Sound FX\" as default world volume is not a good idea because in my opinion it's better to have possibility to slide \"Sound FX\" down from 100% to 10% in loud worlds instead of the next day where you visit all the worlds with 100% \"Sound FX\" that you can barely hear and you are gonna have to change your sound setup, Windows Mixer because it might need to be louder to hear at least something (But then it becomes louder in other games and you are gonna have to lower everything down except VRChat in Windows Mixer or change all other games sound settings), adjust your audio software you might have been using (Adjust OBS settings in case of those who are streaming because of sudden change in Windows mixer and VRChat volume)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5d004bc772b110278e12ba4b",
      "author": {
