      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "One of the several reasons this may be a common occurrence is that it's currently tough to monitor gain staging between Unity's audio source and the ONSP. I made a Canny asking for them to respect changes we make to the native audio mixer so we could try to manage this a little easier (among other cool stuff it'd allow everyone to do). \n\nMaybe VRChat could pack the [Oculus Loudness Meter](https://developer.oculus.com/downloads/package/oculus-audio-loudness-meter/) in with the SDK, and have it auto-run when you do local test builds to encourage staying under a specific loudness target (Oculus recommends -18 LUFS). I think demystifying audio workflows could also really help here too. I'm still hoping for an #audio channel in the discord someday. 🤞",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
