      "value": "@{5a6600a092b3ff44cffeb382|full_name}: Yeah! Audio mixer stuff aside -- you can (sort of) mitigate this by making sure your settings match the attached screenshot in `Project Settings > Audio` and making sure you have 'Spatialize' checked on applicable audio sources. The other culprit is that the ONSP script that gets automatically added when you create a new audio source has it's gain sent to 10db by default, when 0db is unity gain which means it's automatically adding 10db to your audio that you'll only hear at runtime for some reason...so you need to change it down to 0 to ensure levels match between your editor + VRC.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
